  "worked_solution": "The tangent line approximation of $f(x)$ at the point $a=9$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(x) & =f(a)+{f}^{\u2032}(a)(x-a) \\\\  & =f(9)+{f}^{\u2032}(9)(x-9).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that $f(9)=-10,$ and since ${f}^{\u2032}(x)=-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{x}},$ then ${f}^{\u2032}(9)=-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{9}}=-\\frac{2}{3}.$ So, the tangent line approximation is given by\n\n$$\nL(x)=-10-\\frac{2}{3}(x-9).\n$$\n\nNow, we can approximate $f(8.7)$ by evaluating the tangent line approximation at $x=8.7.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(8.7) & \u2248L(8.7) \\\\  & =-10-\\frac{2}{3}(8.7-9) \\\\  & =-10-\\frac{2}{3}(-0.3) \\\\  & =-10+0.2 \\\\  & =-9.8.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
